# Intent: Owner's hands-on test, part 3: the Color Memory beep was not timed with the light. The rule that lights a tile and the one that plays its tone fire together, but the tone reached the codec about 3 ms later while the tile reached the panel 7 to 310 ms later (median 13 ms, measured with the bench: first display flush whose area touches the tile, after the redraw). The tone now waits for that flush and starts from the display's flush-start event for the tile (a 100 ms fallback if no strip comes) and is a pure sine of exactly the lit time, 450 ms (memory.json show, echo and correct are all 450 ms, was 650, 220 and 600), four pitches (E4, C4, G4, A3) made by a recurrence into four PSRAM buffers (58 KB) held only while Color Memory runs. Measured after the change: the tone call is made inside the flush-start event, and the first audio block reaches the codec 0 to 3 ms after that strip starts (4 to 6 ms after the call); the I2S buffer delay is not measured (it needs a microphone). Bench builds log GAMELAT lines (tone call, light asked, flush areas) and LAT game_audio_out.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_games.cc, maipai_games_core.h (ours, G01 to G03) and xiaozhi audio_service.cc (bench mark only)
